    "updated_at": "2015-10-12T07:17:09Z",
    "body": "Should be fine as far as Web compat goes to match IE. Although possibly the spec could be left as is also, though it doesn't match any one browser.\n\nMultiple semicolons or commas:\n\n```\n$ find . -type f -print0 | xargs -0 -P 4 -n 40 grep -iEo \"<meta\\s+[^>]*(http-equiv=[\\\"']?refresh[\\\"']?[^>]+content=[\\\"']\\d+\\s*[;,]\\s*[;,]|content=[\\\"']\\d+\\s*[;,]\\s*[;,][^>]+http-equiv=[\\\"']?refresh[\\\"']?)\" > ../redirect-semicolons.txt\n```\n\nNo matches in webdevdata, also nothing in httparchive.\n\nNo character between at all:\n\n```\n$ find . -type f -print0 | xargs -0 -P 4 -n 40 grep -iEo \"<meta\\s+[^>]*(http-equiv=[\\\"']?refresh[\\\"']?[^>]+content=[\\\"']\\d+url=|content=[\\\"']\\d+url=[^>]+http-equiv=[\\\"']?refresh[\\\"']?)\" > ../redirect-no-space.txt\n```\n\nAlso no matches.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
