    "updated_at": "2015-10-15T18:14:11Z",
    "body": "A different pattern that some pages use is to omit the \"url=\":\n\n```\n./b5/ruby-lang.org_b5bd5513159524a36bd00efdd0824812.html.txt:<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;/en/\" />\n./c0/resume.se_c0678d3958ceba143b5122f3fa6c5722.html.txt:<meta http-equiv=\"Refresh\" content=\"600;?ar=true\" />\n./ca/ponisha.ir_caa8c6615e8316fab4ac2c2df25e636b.html.txt:<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0; /error.php?code=nojava\" />\n./cf/bd-pratidin.com_cf3d93daee2cc94d6c89200a87935b1b.ascii:<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;http://www.bd-pratidin.com/\" />\n```\n\nview-source:https://www.ruby-lang.org/ uses a script to redirect and meta refresh in a `noscript`. The others appear to have changed since.\n\n(Total 1422 pages with a meta refresh; out of 87,000 pages.)\n\nhttp://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/3679\n`<meta http-equiv=\"refresh\" content=\"0;/en/\" />`\nIE11 refreshes but ignores the part after the \";\". Gecko/WebKit/Blink redirect to the string after the \";\".\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
